---
import editorShot from "../assets/screens/editor.webp";
import paletteShot from "../assets/screens/palette.webp";
---

<section class="section" id="interface">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">A familiar interface</p>
      <h2>Two panes, native controls, no surprises</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        The same patterns as your file manager: select, drag and drop. The queue
        reports what the protocol is actually doing instead of drawing a guess.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="shot-grid">
      <figure class="shot shot-square">
        <div class="shot-media">
          <img
            src={editorShot.src}
            width={editorShot.width}
            height={editorShot.height}
            alt="Editor with design-notes.md open on the remote server"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Edit remote files in place</strong>
          <span>Atomic saves and stale-write detection.</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="shot shot-square">
        <div class="shot-media">
          <img
            src={paletteShot.src}
            width={paletteShot.width}
            height={paletteShot.height}
            alt="Command palette searching for connections and actions"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Every action one keystroke away</strong>
          <span>⌘K opens the command palette.</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
